if (typeof(Window.HWND) == "undefined") Window.HWND = 0;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// windowEx.dll emulation: the complete public surface, ported from the
// official plugin (wamsoft/windowEx main.cpp + manual.tjs) to a console.
//
// The Kirikiroid2 1.3.9 packages that game distributions actually ship for
// statically include a windowEx.dll port, which is why titles built for them
// call this API without a fallback (ECPlugin titles read
// System.getMonitorInfo during KAG boot) or probe it to select WindowEx-only
// branches (KAGEX titles: window control menu, pseudo fullscreen, placement).
// The stock zeas2/Kirikiroid2 source tree has neither port, so this layer
// publishes the full member set for every title -- nothing here is gated per
// game.  What a console cannot do (move/resize native chrome, native menus)
// is inert; what can be answered (a single fixed display, its metrics, the
// window geometry that display implies) returns real values.
//
// Member meanings follow the plugin manual; the fixed display is 1920x1080
// with no taskbar, so work == monitor.  Rect dictionaries are %[ x, y, w, h ],
// the same shape the plugin returns.
//
// Not ported (Windows-only plumbing with no console counterpart, and no
// title in the verified set reads them): findWindowEx / classLongPtr /
// loadCursor / mapVirtualKey -> inert stubs below, IME control, overlay
// bitmaps, message hooks and hotkey delivery (registration answers are
// retained; no native events can fire on a console).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

